    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1844"
                            type="person">Mrs. Else Staudinger</rs>
                        <lb/>American Comittee for Refugee Scholars, Writers &amp; Artists <lb/>66
                        Fifth Avenue <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York
                            City</rs>
                    </fw><dateline><date when="1946-01-29">January 29, 1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1844" type="person">Mrs.
                            Staudinger</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Referring to our telephone conversation I would like to ask you again for help
                    for <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1673" type="person">Mr. Hans Sahl</rs>.</p>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1673" type="person">Hans Sahl</rs> is known to me
                    for many years. He is one of the few German poets and writers who deserves
                    special attention and all assistance possible. His talent and his abilities are
                    far above average, and I am convinced that his novel is one of the few
                    worthwhile to be published. For that reason he should be supported at least for
                    another 2 months in order to enable him to continue his novel.</p>
                <p>I know that you generously have assisted him a year ago and I sincerely hope that
                    you will help him a second time to fulfill his task.</p>
                <p>Thanking you in anticipation for all you can do,</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours very sincerely,</salute>
                    <signed><unclear reason="illegible"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                                type="person">P. Tillich</rs></unclear> <lb/>Professor at Union
                        Theological Seminary, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York
                            City</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
